! The `pw.x` reference leg for the relaxed magnetocrystalline anisotropy, moment
! along x (angle1 = 90): `co-tetragonal-relaxed-mae.in` with the direction set here and
! `conv_thr` tightened to 1e-12, which is the threshold `PLAN.md` P87's number was
! taken at. Run serially with `pw.x` 7.5 on 2026-09-23; its output is
! `reference.out.co-tetragonal-relaxed-mae-x` beside it. The two cardinal axes of
! a tetragonal crystal are stationary directions of the anisotropy energy, so
! nothing has to hold the moment for the run to converge where it was put.
&control
   calculation = 'scf'
/
&system
   ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 4.60, celldm(3) = 1.30, nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
   noncolin = .true., lspinorb = .true., nosym = .true.,
   ecutwfc = 20.0, ecutrho = 160.0,
   occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'mv', degauss = 0.02,
   starting_magnetization(1) = 0.6,
   angle1(1) = 90.0, angle2(1) = 0.0,
/
&electrons
   conv_thr = 1.0e-12
   mixing_beta = 0.3, electron_maxstep = 300
/
ATOMIC_SPECIES
Co 58.933 Co.rel-pbe-nd-rrkjus.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
Co 0.0 0.0 0.0
K_POINTS automatic
3 3 2 0 0 0
